{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-29_bldr-ex99_1.htm, sha256 58f89a6138c740544ff1f16c1509da84698488280f7d0d2f98449f6cd81c3434.\nEX-99.1 2 bldr-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1\nFor Immediate Release\nBuilders FirstSource Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results\nOctober 29, 2026 (Irving, TX) \u2013 Builders FirstSource, Inc. (NYSE: BLDR) today reported its results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026.\nThird Quarter 2026 Highlights\nAll Year-Over-Year Comparisons Unless Otherwise Noted:\n\u2022 Net sales were $3.9 billion, a decrease of 2.2%, primarily due to a lower housing starts environment and related headwinds. The decline reflects lower core organic net sales as well as commodity deflation, partially offset by growth from acquisitions. \u2022 Gross profit was $1.1 billion, a decrease of 10.6%. Gross profit margin percentage decreased 260 basis points to 27.8%, primarily driven by a lower housing starts environment and related headwinds. \u2022 Net income was $60.4 million, or diluted EPS of $0.56 compared to diluted EPS of $1.10 in the prior year period. Net income as a percent of net sales decreased by 150 basis points to 1.6%. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA decreased 28.3% to $311.1 million, primarily driven by lower gross profit. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA margin declined by 290 basis points to 8.1%, attributable to lower gross margin and reduced operating leverage. \u2022 Cash provided by operating activities was $146.6 million, a decrease of $401.2 million compared to the prior year period. The Company's free cash flow was $76.0 million, a decrease of 83.7%, compared to $464.9 million in the prior year period. The decrease was primarily driven by lower net income and higher net working capital, partially offset by lower capital expenditures.\n\u201cOur third quarter results reflect the disciplined execution of our team and the resilience of our platform. While housing market conditions remain challenging, we are focused on what we can control: delivering solutions that help builders operate more efficiently and investing in value-added products and technology to drive productivity and fuel growth. These efforts are reinforcing our leadership position and our role as the partner of choice for homebuilders,\u201d commented Peter Jackson, CEO of Builders FirstSource.\nMr. Jackson continued, \u201cThis environment underscores the importance of operational excellence and differentiated capabilities at scale. Our investments in value-added offerings and technology strengthen our competitive advantages and position us to outperform as housing market conditions improve.\u201d\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Pete Beckmann, CFO of Builders FirstSource, added, \u201cOur third quarter results met our expectations, reflecting solid execution and a sustained focus on cost management. Based on our year-to-date performance, we are narrowing our full-year outlook and maintaining the midpoints for net sales and Adjusted EBITDA as we enter the final quarter. Our strong capital position and solid cash flow generation give us the capacity to pursue growth opportunities while maintaining financial flexibility.\u201d\n1\nThird Quarter 2026 Financial Performance Highlights\nAll Year-Over-Year Comparisons Unless Otherwise Noted:\nNet Sales\n\u2022 Net sales were $3.9 billion, a decrease of 2.2%, primarily due to a lower housing starts environment and related headwinds. The decrease reflects a 3.9% decline in core organic net sales, as well as commodity deflation of 0.1%, partially offset by growth from acquisitions of 1.8%. \u2022 Core organic net sales declined 3.9%. Single Family declined 6.2%, Multi-Family increased 2.0%, and Repair and Remodel (\u201cR&R\u201d)/Other increased 0.3%. On a weighted basis, Single Family lowered net sales by 4.3%, Multi-Family increased sales by 0.2%, and R&R/Other increased sales by 0.2%.\nGross Profit\n\u2022 Gross profit was $1.1 billion, a decrease of 10.6%. Gross profit margin percentage decreased 260 basis points to 27.8%, primarily driven by a lower housing starts environment and related headwinds.\nSelling, General and Administrative Expenses\n\u2022 SG&A was $973.2 million, an increase of $2.5 million, or 0.3%, primarily driven by additional expenses from operations acquired within the last twelve months and higher fuel and insurance expenses, partially offset by lower variable compensation as a result of decreased net sales and lower wages as a result of cost saving actions. As a percentage of net sales, total SG&A increased by 70 basis points to 25.3%, primarily attributable to reduced operating leverage.\nNet Interest Expense\n\u2022 Net interest expense increased $3.0 million to $72.2 million, primarily due to additional interest expense from other finance obligations and higher average debt balances.\nIncome Tax Expense (Benefit)\n\u2022 Income tax was $(33.6) million, compared to $37.1 million in the prior year period. The decrease in income tax expense was primarily driven by losses before income taxes incurred by certain subsidiaries in the current year period, as well as lower consolidated income before income taxes.\nNet Income\n\u2022 Net income was $60.4 million, or $0.56 earnings per diluted share, compared to net income of $122.4 million, or $1.10 earnings per diluted share, in the prior year period. The decrease in net income was primarily driven by lower gross profit and higher net interest and SG&A expenses, partially offset by an income tax benefit.\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "\u2022 Net income as a percentage of net sales was 1.6%, a decrease of 150 basis points from the prior year period, primarily due to lower gross profit margin and higher net interest and SG&A expenses, partially offset by an income tax benefit.\n2\nAdjusted Net Income\n\u2022 Adjusted net income was $162.2 million, a decrease of 26.9%, primarily driven by lower gross profit and higher net interest expense, partially offset by lower adjusted SG&A and an income tax benefit.\nAdjusted Earnings Per Diluted Share\n\u2022 Adjusted earnings per diluted share was $1.51, compared to $2.00 in the prior year period. The 24.5% decrease was primarily driven by lower adjusted net income, partially offset by share repurchases.\nAdjusted EBITDA\n\u2022 Adjusted EBITDA decreased 28.3% to $311.1 million, primarily driven by lower gross profit. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA margin declined by 290 basis points from the prior year period to 8.1%, primarily due to lower gross profit margin and reduced operating leverage.\nCapital Structure, Leverage, and Liquidity Information\n\u2022 For the three months ended September 30, 2026, cash provided by operating activities was $146.6 million, and cash used in investing activities was $188.3 million. The Company's free cash flow was $76.0 million, compared to $464.9 million in the prior year period, largely the result of lower net income and higher net working capital, partially offset by lower capital expenditures. \u2022 Liquidity as of September 30, 2026, was $1.5 billion, consisting of approximately $1.4 billion in net borrowing availability under the revolving credit facility and $0.1 billion of cash on hand. \u2022 As of September 30, 2026, LTM Adjusted EBITDA was $1.1 billion and net debt was $4.6 billion, resulting in a net debt to LTM Adjusted EBITDA ratio of 4.1x, compared to 2.3x in the prior year period. \u2022 The Company has $500 million remaining under its share repurchase authorization. \u2022 Since the inception of its buyback program in August 2021, the Company has repurchased 102.6 million shares of its common stock, or 49.7% of its total shares outstanding, at an average price of $81.26 per share for a total cost of $8.3 billion, inclusive of applicable fees and taxes.\nProductivity Savings From Operational Excellence\n\u2022 For the third quarter, the Company delivered approximately $23 million in productivity savings related to operational excellence and supply chain initiatives. \u2022 Year to date, the Company has delivered approximately $57 million in productivity savings. \u2022 The Company expects to deliver $60 million to $70 million in productivity savings in 2026.\n2026 Full Year Total Company Outlook\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "For 2026, the Company expects to achieve the financial performance highlighted below. Projected Net Sales and Adjusted EBITDA include the expected impact of price, commodities, and margins. We are not providing a quantitative reconciliation of our forward-looking guidance of adjusted EBITDA, adjusted EBITDA margin, or free cash flow because we are unable to predict with reasonable certainty all the\n3\ncomponents required to provide such reconciliation without unreasonable efforts, which are uncertain and could have a material impact on GAAP reported results for the guidance period. See \u201cNon-GAAP Financial Measures\u201d for additional information.\n\u2022 Net Sales to be in a range of $14.2 billion to $14.6 billion. \u2022 Gross Profit margin to be in a range of 27.5% to 28.5%. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA to be in a range of $1.075 billion to $1.125 billion. \u2022 Adjusted EBITDA margin to be in a range of 7.4% to 7.9%. \u2022 Free cash flow of approximately $400 million to $450 million, assuming average commodity prices in the range of $390 to $410 per thousand board foot (mbf).\n2026 Full Year Assumptions\nThe Company\u2019s anticipated 2026 performance is based on several assumptions for the full year, including the following:\n\u2022 Within the Company\u2019s geographies, Single Family starts are projected to be down mid- to high-single digits, Multi-Family starts are projected to be down mid-single digits, and Repair & Remodel activity is projected to be down 1%. \u2022 Acquisitions completed within the last twelve months are projected to add net sales growth in the range of 1.5% to 2%. \u2022 Total capital expenditures in the range of $175 million to $225 million. \u2022 Interest expense in the range of $290 million to $300 million. \u2022 Depreciation and amortization expenses in the range of $580 million to $610 million. \u2022 No change in selling days versus 2025.\nConference Call\nBuilders FirstSource will host a conference call and webcast on Thursday, October 29, 2026, to discuss the Company\u2019s financial results and other business matters. The teleconference will begin at 8:00 a.m. Central Time and will be hosted by Peter Jackson, Chief Executive Officer, and Pete Beckmann, Chief Financial Officer.\nThe live webcast, archived replay, and the accompanying presentation can be accessed on the Company's investor relations website at investors.bldr.com under the Events and Presentations section. The online archive of the webcast will be available for approximately 90 days.\nTo participate in the teleconference, please dial into the call a few minutes before the start time at 800-420-1459 (U.S. and Canada) or 203-518-9861 (international), Conference ID: BLDRQ326.\nUpcoming Events\n"}
{"page": 5, "text": "The Company will host an Investor Day at the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) in New York on Tuesday, November 17, 2026, with the formal schedule beginning at 8:45 a.m. Eastern Time. The event will feature presentations by the executive management team and multiple Q&A sessions. A live webcast and an archived copy of the webcast will be made available on investors.bldr.com under the Events and Presentations section. Additionally, the Company will participate in investor meetings at the Goldman Sachs Industrials and Materials Conference in New York City on December 3.\n4\nAbout Builders FirstSource\nBuilders FirstSource (NYSE: BLDR), headquartered in Irving, Texas, is a leading provider of building materials for professional builders in new residential construction and repair and remodeling. We deliver integrated homebuilding solutions by manufacturing, supplying, and installing a full range of structural and related building products. With approximately 575 locations across 43 states, we serve 48 of the top 50 and 91 of the top 100 Core Based Statistical Areas (CBSAs), ensuring broad geographic coverage and enhancing our ability to partner with our customers. Our leading network of strategically located manufacturing facilities produces factory-built roof and floor trusses, wall panels, vinyl windows, custom millwork and trim, manufactured and semi-custom modular homes, as well as engineered wood that we design and cut specifically for each home. We also assemble interior and exterior doors into pre-hung units for easy installation. Additionally, we distribute a wide range of building products, including lumber, sheet goods, windows, doors, millwork, and specialty items. Our services, which vary by market, include professional installation, turnkey framing, and shell construction. Supported by the latest construction innovations and digital solutions, we help drive greater efficiency across homebuilding. Learn more at www.bldr.com\nForward-Looking Statements\n"}
